\textbf{Solution}: From (1) it is known that $B(3, 0)$. Assume the equation of line $BC$ is: $y=kx+b$. Substituting $B(3, 0)$, $C(0, 3)$, we get: \[
\begin{cases}
3k+b=0 \\
b=3
\end{cases}
\], solving this system gives: \[
\begin{cases}
k=-1 \\
b=3
\end{cases}
\]. Therefore, the equation of line $BC$ is $y=-x+3$, thus $M(m, -m+3)$. Furthermore, since $MN \perp x$ axis, hence $N(m, -m^2+2m+3)$, therefore $MN=\boxed{-m^2+3m}$ $(0<m<3)$.
